<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Snoop (245)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>snoop &lt;player&gt;
snoop               (stop snooping)
</pre>
<p>Lets you see everything a player sees, as it happens to them. Only one 
god can snoop a player at a time ("Busy already."), and only a player of 
a lower level than yours, who is connected. The player isn't told. It is 
logged.
</p><p>Snooping intrudes on a player's privacy. The players' help sets out the 
promises the administrators make about it (see <a cmd='#'>Help Snoop</a>): ask for 
permission when you can, use it only for the rules, security and 
debugging, and keep what you see confidential.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Snoop</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Plog</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Switch</a>
</pre>




</div>